WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.370
Speaker 1: All right, we are going to be talking
today about the Pandora papers much requested

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.799
segment that'll be coming up.

00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:11.840
I want to start with Facebook, Instagram and
WhatsApp because yesterday Facebook and associated

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:18.441
owned apps and platforms WhatsApp and Instagram
suffered a complete and total outage, their

00:00:18.441 --> 00:00:21.340
worst in a very long time.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:29.910
Just hours after a Facebook whistleblower
was revealed and also made some very, very

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:37.430
disturbing claims about Facebook's awareness
about negative influence on people and society.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:44.750
But putting, according to the whistleblower,
profit over society, profit over people.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:51.530
Now are the two stories connected rampant
speculation that the outage was deliberately

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:58.520
put in place by Facebook to prevent those
very platforms from being used to spread the

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.110
claims of the whistleblower.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.110
The timing is definitely interesting, for
sure.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.080
There was no denying it.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.270
Although at this point in time, we don't have
anything specific that would tell us that

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:09.270
that's what went on.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.520
Some people are saying, David, what do you
need?

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.520
What do you need?

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.670
That's more specific.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.600
Let's look at the two stories sort of in tandem.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:22.130
First and foremost, Facebook whistleblower
revealed on 60 Minutes says the company prioritized

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:27.170
profit over public good would not come as
a surprise to many people that that's what

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.409
Facebook did.

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:34.780
If indeed, that is what the whistleblower
observed the identity of the Facebook whistleblower,

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.950
who released tens of thousands of pages of
internal research and documents leading to

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:44.009
a firestorm for the social media company in
recent weeks, was revealed on 60 Minutes Sunday

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:50.550
night as Frances Horgan, the 37 year old former
Facebook product manager who worked on civic

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:56.259
integrity issues at the company, says the
documents show that Facebook knows its platforms

00:01:56.259 --> 00:02:02.720
are used to spread hate, violence and misinformation,
and that the company has tried to hide that

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:03.970
evidence.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:09.269
Reminds me of ExxonMobil knowing in the 70s
the impact on the environment that their drilling

00:02:09.269 --> 00:02:12.430
activity had very similar vibes.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:17.859
The thing I saw at Facebook over and over
again was there were conflicts of interest

00:02:17.859 --> 00:02:22.889
between what was good for the public and what
was good for Facebook and Facebook over and

00:02:22.889 --> 00:02:29.599
over again chose to optimize for its own interests,
like making more money, Hogan told 60 Minutes.

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:34.430
60 Minutes correspondent Scott Pelley quoted
one internal Facebook document as saying quote,

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:38.829
We have evidence from a variety of sources
that hate speech, divisive political speech

00:02:38.829 --> 00:02:44.340
and misinformation on Facebook and the family
of apps are affecting societies around the

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:45.599
world.

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:50.390
About a month ago, Horgan filed at least eight
complaints, with the FCC alleging the company

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.309
is hiding research about its shortcomings
from investors and the public.

00:02:54.309 --> 00:02:58.120
She shared the documents with The Wall Street
Journal, which published a multi-part investigation

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.420
showing Facebook was aware of problems with
its apps, including the negative effects of

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:06.330
misinformation and the harm caused, especially
to young girls by Instagram.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.500
If you're interested in that specifically,
check out some of Jonathan Height's work on

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:16.150
the effect of social media, not just on young
people in general, but disproportionately

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:19.620
on young girls, something he's worked on quite
a bit.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:26.370
Hagen, who started at Facebook in 2019, is
set to testify today before the Senate Subcommittee

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.529
on Consumer Protection, Product Safety and
Data Security.

00:03:29.529 --> 00:03:33.419
I've seen a bunch of social networks and it
was substantially worse at Facebook than anything

00:03:33.419 --> 00:03:34.749
I've seen before.

00:03:34.749 --> 00:03:39.049
At some point in twenty one, I realized I'm
going to have to do this in a systemic way

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:42.879
that I'm going to have to get out enough documents
that no one can question.

00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:43.879
This is real.

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:47.689
Facebook has pushed back against reports claiming
the claims are misleading and arguing its

00:03:47.689 --> 00:03:49.739
apps do more good than harm.

00:03:49.739 --> 00:03:52.579
So we're going to get back to that in a moment.

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:59.419
Simultaneously, almost with the unveiling
of this whistleblower Facebook suffering its

00:03:59.419 --> 00:04:04.439
worst outage since 2008, pulling down Instagram,
pulling down WhatsApp as well.

00:04:04.439 --> 00:04:08.809
Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp shut down
for more than six hours on Monday.

00:04:08.809 --> 00:04:14.979
It marked the worst outage for the tech giant
since 2008, when a bug knocked Facebook offline

00:04:14.979 --> 00:04:20.359
for about a day, but the service had only
80 million users back then.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:26.169
The outage was caused by quote configuration
changes on the backbone routers.

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:33.180
Facebook's VP of Infrastructure Santosh Janardhan,
said in a blog post late Monday.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:36.680
As of the writing of this article, some of
the services are not yet fully functioning.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:41.960
For example, some users are still reporting
problems posting new content to Instagram.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.759
All three platforms stopped working shortly
before noon, when websites and apps for Facebook

00:04:46.759 --> 00:04:49.680
services were responding with server errors.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.430
Reports on DownDetector dot com showed the
outages appeared to be widespread.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.789
OK, so a bunch of interesting things here.

00:04:56.789 --> 00:04:58.370
The first thing is again, are these.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.280
Two stories connected, is this a lie?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.830
Is Facebook just straight up lying?

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:09.840
And they pulled down access to their their
platforms specifically to prevent the spread

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.520
of the information about the whistleblower?

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.760
I don't know.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:17.180
I mean, you know, this is one of those things
where there are people who will say, obviously

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.280
not, that's obviously not what happened.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.690
Others who will say, of course, that's what
happened.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:28.490
This is an outage of this degree is so rare
that the idea that it would just be a coincidence

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.870
is essentially impossible.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.651
And then people with opinions in between,
I don't know.

00:05:32.651 --> 00:05:35.490
All I can tell you is the timing is interesting
now.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:42.750
What was more interesting is that I missed
nothing from these platforms being down.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.900
And what I mean by that is, OK.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:45.900
I was working.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.319
I don't really do Facebook during the day.

00:05:48.319 --> 00:05:54.050
It didn't affect me negatively in any way
that Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp were

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.819
down for this period of time.

00:05:55.819 --> 00:05:58.840
Maybe if it had been a Saturday when I might
just be chatting with people on some of these

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.780
platforms, maybe it would have been different.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.280
It did affect our team.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.060
We upload content to these platforms.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.460
We were unable to do so.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.629
It kind of threw for a loop our entire day.

00:06:08.629 --> 00:06:14.620
But it is very interesting to get perspective,
sometimes on the importance we believe that

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:19.400
these apps have and then what they really
have when they are missing now.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:26.810
WhatsApp is relied upon in many countries
as the default messaging app, and I am on

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:30.669
a bunch of WhatsApp threads with people in
other countries, Argentina and elsewhere.

00:06:30.669 --> 00:06:32.240
Obviously, those aren't working.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.389
I'm not using that to communicate things of
paramount importance.

00:06:35.389 --> 00:06:37.300
Many people are in it, affected them significantly.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:43.569
Now, Congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez
is using what happened yesterday as an opportunity

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.590
to say break these companies up.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.960
There's no reason WhatsApp should have to
be down because Facebook is down other than

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.779
Facebook bought WhatsApp because it saw WhatsApp
as a competitor.

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:56.300
We will deal with that on the bonus show,
but in the meantime, let me know your thoughts.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:08:06.830
Do you see the outage and the whistleblower
unveiling as connected or merely coincidental?

